course: dictionary
lesson: 10542
title: Sounds too high to hear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some sounds are too high-pitched for people to hear, and scientists call these sounds ultrasound. «Most bat calls are ultrasound, too high for grown-ups to hear.» The clue is in the words too high: the sound is there, but our ears cannot pick it up.
explain: Ultrasound is also a medical word. «Ultrasound uses sound waves to show a baby inside its mother.» Here an ultrasound is a scan, a test that makes a picture of the inside of the body.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is used. Ask yourself: is this about hearing, or about a medical test? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Ultrasound is sound that is too high-pitched for humans to hear.
fact: Bats and dogs can hear ultrasound, but people cannot.
fact: An ultrasound scan uses sound waves to make a picture of the inside of the body, often a baby before it is born.
fact: Ultrasound is also used in some cleaning machines and medical treatments.
fact: An ultrasound scan is safe and does not use X-rays.
exercise: «Most bat calls are ultrasound, too high for grown-ups to hear.» What does ultrasound mean here? | Very loud sound that breaks glass | Quiet music | *Sound too high for people to hear | A picture of the inside of the body
exercise: Doctors use an ultrasound to look inside the body. What is an ultrasound scan? | A loud alarm in a hospital | A type of X-ray | *A medical test that uses sound waves to make a picture | A kind of bat
exercise: «Mice call to each other in sounds too high for people to hear, called ultrasound.» Which word names this kind of sound? | people | mice | call | *ultrasound
test: «A new baby had an ultrasound before it was born.» What does the ultrasound most likely show? | What the baby is thinking | The colour of the nurse's shoes | *The inside of the body, as a picture | The weather outside the hospital
test: Which of these can hear ultrasound? | A teacher reading aloud | A grown-up person | *A bat
exam: «Ships use echoes under water, called sonar, and doctors use very high sounds, called ultrasound, to see inside the body.» What is ultrasound? | A kind of ship | *Very high sound used to see inside the body | Water that echoes | A slow, deep sound
